A sister site already has this pattern. Clone https://github.com/helloautomize-cell/drmalathi into a temp folder OUTSIDE this repo and read these files (read-only, copy patterns, not content or branding): lib/booking-schema.ts, lib/google-sheets.ts, lib/booking-pipeline.ts, lib/booking-action.ts, components/forms/booking-fields.tsx, components/forms/booking-form-controller.tsx, components/forms/contact-fallback-panel.tsx, tests/booking.test.ts. Medcare differs in three ways: it has hourly slots with live availability, the capacity check happens inside the Apps Script (one "book" call, not "recent" + "append"), and there's no Resend email for bookings.

1. SEARCH FIRST
Before editing, search the whole repo (outside the read-only resources/ folder) for: the current "Book Appointment" / "Request appointment" form(s) and the server action or API route they post to; every link or button that says "Book Appointment" or points to the booking form or #book; the "Reason for visit" options; the site config that holds the phone (60031 21297) and WhatsApp numbers (60031 21297, 93651 75235); .env.example; lib/schema.ts; lib/llms.ts; the privacy page. Reuse the existing site config values and don't hard-code numbers twice.

2. APPS SCRIPT CONTRACT (server only)
POST JSON to process.env.SHEETS_WEBHOOK_URL with redirect "follow", cache "no-store", a 15 s AbortController timeout, Content-Type application/json. Every body includes secret: process.env.SHEETS_WEBHOOK_SECRET. Both env vars are server only, never NEXT_PUBLIC_, and never logged.

a) Availability
   request:  { action: "availability", from: "YYYY-MM-DD", days: 1..31, secret }
   response: { ok: true, today: "YYYY-MM-DD", lastDate: "YYYY-MM-DD",
               dates: [ { date, closed: boolean, reason: string,
                          slots: [ { start: "HH:mm", end: "HH:mm", label: "11 am to 12 pm",
                                     capacity: number, left: number, open: boolean } ] } ] }
   or { ok: false }. "open" already accounts for capacity, holidays and the same-day lead time. Only open slots can be chosen.

b) Book
   request:  { action: "book", secret, booking: { id, source, name, mobile, visitType, reason,
               date: "YYYY-MM-DD", slotStart: "HH:mm", notes, consent: "v1" } }
   response: { ok: true, code: "ok", slot: "<label>" }
          or { ok: false, code: "slot_full" | "slot_closed" | "duplicate" | "limit" | "busy" | "invalid" }
          or { ok: false } (bad secret or error).

3. SERVER CODE
- lib/booking-schema.ts (zod, shared by client and server): name trimmed 2 to 60; mobile normalised exactly like the reference normalizeMobile (10-digit Indian mobile, or an international number of 10 to 15 digits); visitType one of the four in section 4; reason must be one of the options for that visit type; date YYYY-MM-DD from today to today + 30 in Asia/Kolkata; slotStart HH:mm; notes trimmed, max 300, optional; consent literal true. Include istDateString, addDays and maskMobile helpers like the reference.
- lib/google-sheets.ts: sheetsConfigured(), getAvailability(from, days), bookSlot(booking). Cache availability in memory for 30 s per from+days key and clear the cache after every book call. Throw on HTTP, JSON or timeout errors. Callers catch.
- lib/booking-action.ts ("use server"):
  - getSlots(from: string, days: number): validates input (days 1 to 14), returns the availability result or { ok: false }. If the Sheet can't be reached, return { ok: false, offline: true }. The UI then shows the clinic's standard slots as selectable from data/booking-options.ts, and the final book call still checks capacity.
  - submitBooking(formData): pipeline in this order: honeypot field "website" filled → silently return ok; startedAt missing or under 3 s → silently return ok; zod parse fails → generic error; generate id "bk_" + 8 chars from node:crypto randomInt; source is code-defined ("website-book", "website-home" or "website-contact", depending on which surface submitted, never trusted from the URL); call bookSlot.
  - Map the result: ok → { ok: true, bookingId, mobile (masked in UI), date, slotLabel }. slot_full / slot_closed → { ok: false, reason: "slot_unavailable" }. duplicate → { ok: false, reason: "duplicate" }. Anything else, including thrown errors → { ok: false, reason: "failed" }.
  - Development only: when the env vars are missing and NODE_ENV !== "production", getSlots returns every standard slot as open with left = 4, and submitBooking returns a fake success with id bk_dev0000. In production with missing env, return failed.
  - Never console.log form values in production.
- If the current booking form sends email (Resend or similar), remove that from the booking flow only. Leave other forms alone.

